{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Hollow Ledger","logline":"When a Drift Cartel toll-master is found murdered on a skybridge with only wind-debt marks and a missing ledger as clues, cartographer Veya and the ruthless toll-master Kael race to find the ledger before it can expose, or bury, the truth behind the Toll War.","theme":"Truth hoarded becomes a weapon; truth shared becomes a bridge.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Body on the Bridge","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_body_on_bridge","title":"The Body on the Bridge","summary":"Veya, surveying a failing span, finds a Cartel toll-keeper dead at the Mistral Docks bridge head. Strange wind-debt marks are scored into the cloudstone beside the body, and the toll ledger's clasp lies empty.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to record the damaged span and understand what the wind-debt marks mean.","conflict":"Kael arrives first as the Cartel's toll-master and tries to seal the scene, claiming jurisdiction, while Veya's stubborn curiosity keeps her at the marks.","outcome":"Kael grudgingly allows Veya to copy the marks to prove the Wardens are not to blame, but he privately resolves to find the missing ledger first."},{"id":"scn_reading_the_marks","title":"Reading the Marks","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya uses her wind-sight and the academy's archives to study the copied marks. They record unpaid wind-debts, but in a pattern that implies the debts were forged.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Decode the wind-debt marks to learn who owed the dead keeper.","conflict":"Her certainty that the marks point to the Cartel blinds her to details that do not fit, and she dismisses a contradicting entry rather than admit a possible error.","outcome":"She concludes the debts were falsified from a ledger and that the missing book is the key, but she overlooks that the marks also name a Hollow grain account.","depends_on":["scn_body_on_bridge"]},{"id":"scn_kael_closes_ranks","title":"Kael Closes Ranks","summary":"Kael convenes the Cartel's toll clerks at the docks and demands a search for the ledger, while pressing the Wardens' supply accusations to deflect suspicion from the Cartel.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Recover the ledger quietly and secure the Cartel's hold on the remaining stable routes.","conflict":"His clerks fear the murder was an inside job, and Kael's habit of valuing people by price makes them doubt his loyalty to them.","outcome":"A clerk privately tells Kael that grain-levy debts in the ledger were altered, sending him toward The Hollow and raising the stakes of the Grain Levy."},{"id":"scn_maris_hidden_route","title":"A Smuggler's Warning","summary":"Maris, moving smuggled grain through the service corridors of The Hollow, finds a cloth-wrapped book hidden in a granary, but cannot yet read it, and hears that Cartel enforcers are asking questions.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Keep the Hollow's smuggled grain flowing despite the enforcers closing in.","conflict":"Her slow trust makes her hide the book rather than tell anyone, even though it may endanger her isle.","outcome":"Maris conceals the ledger-like book and decides to trust only Veya with it, setting up a risky meeting.","depends_on":["scn_kael_closes_ranks"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Debts and Deceptions","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_veya_seeks_maris","title":"Veya Seeks Maris","summary":"Veya travels to The Hollow after finding the grain account in the marks. She trades wind-current knowledge for Maris's secret paths and learns Maris has a hidden book.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Find whoever holds the grain account named in the marks.","conflict":"Maris distrusts the Wardens' cartographer and refuses to hand over the book without proof Veya will not give it to the Cartel.","outcome":"Maris lets Veya read the book. It is the missing ledger, with pages torn out and altered levy entries.","depends_on":["scn_reading_the_marks","scn_maris_hidden_route"]},{"id":"scn_torn_pages","title":"The Torn Pages","summary":"Veya and Maris compare the ledger against Veya's decoded marks and find that the missing pages cover the Cartel's levy figures and a Warden-signed supply order from Emberroost.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Work out who altered the entries and why the keeper was killed.","conflict":"The Warden signature implicates Veya's own faction, and Veya's refusal to admit she may have been wrong about the Cartel causes a bitter argument with Maris.","outcome":"They agree to take the ledger to Emberroost to verify the signature, but Maris warns Veya she will not forgive betrayal."},{"id":"scn_emberroost_forge","title":"Cables at Emberroost","summary":"At the forge-island, Veya and Maris question Warden engineers about the supply order. They discover cloudstone shipments were deliberately delayed, weakening the spans around Mistral Docks.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Verify the signature and learn who delayed the supplies.","conflict":"The Wardens, wary of outsiders after Kael's sabotage accusations, close ranks and refuse to open their records.","outcome":"A junior engineer admits the delays were ordered through Cartel intermediaries, which means the Cartel profited from the failing bridges and someone forged the Warden signature.","depends_on":["scn_torn_pages"]},{"id":"scn_kael_tracks_the_ledger","title":"Kael Tracks the Ledger","summary":"Kael follows enforcer reports to Emberroost and corners Veya and Maris at the shielded forge-pits, demanding the ledger.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants the ledger and Veya's charts before either can be used against the Cartel.","conflict":"Open flame is forbidden outside the forge-pits, so Kael's enforcers cannot use fire to intimidate them, and Kael's admiration for Veya makes him hesitate to harm her.","outcome":"Maris leads Veya out through unmapped service corridors, but Kael keeps one torn page, learning that someone inside the Cartel forged the debts.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_forge"]},{"id":"scn_kael_doubts","title":"A Price Too High","summary":"Back at Mistral Docks, Kael confronts the clerk who gave him the levy tip and realises a Cartel rival used his own monopoly push to cover the murder and the forgery.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Identify who forged the debts inside the Cartel.","conflict":"Naming the culprit would break the Cartel's unity, which conflicts with his goal of securing the monopoly.","outcome":"Kael learns the killer plans to cut the Mistral Docks span to destroy the evidence, and he chooses to warn Veya through a rival's channel rather than use the knowledge for himself.","depends_on":["scn_kael_tracks_the_ledger"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_confession","title":"The Wrong Chart","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and finds that her own charts, which she refused to correct earlier, misplaced the failing span. Admitting the error is painful, but it reveals where the killer will strike.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Chart a safe route to protect the spans before they collapse.","conflict":"Veya's flaw delays her acceptance of the error, and Maris, fearing betrayal, threatens to leave with the ledger.","outcome":"Veya admits she was wrong, earns Maris's cautious trust, and they race to Mistral Docks with the corrected chart and the ledger.","depends_on":["scn_kael_doubts","scn_torn_pages"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Span Breaks","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_showdown_at_the_span","title":"Showdown at the Span","summary":"On the Mistral Docks skybridge, Veya, Maris and Kael confront the Cartel factor who forged the debts and killed the toll keeper. The span is rigged to be severed by a single spark.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Expose the killer with the ledger and stop the span from being cut.","conflict":"The killer holds a hidden spark-lamp against the no-open-flame rule, and Kael must choose between protecting Cartel unity and the truth, while Veya fears the ledger will make her as ambitious as the Cartel.","outcome":"Veya reads the corrected wind-sight warning, Maris leads the crowd off the span through the service corridors, and Kael publicly reads the forged entries, which exposes the killer.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_confession","scn_kael_doubts"]},{"id":"scn_the_bridge_holds","title":"The Bridge Holds","summary":"As the killer's spark threatens the cables, Veya's chart guides Kael and Maris to shift the load and shield the lamp, and the span holds.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Save the span and the crowd before the spark severs it.","conflict":"Saving the span requires Kael to give up the monopoly leverage the broken bridge would have handed the Cartel.","outcome":"Kael chooses the bridge over control, the killer is seized by Wardens and clerks, and the ledger is recovered intact.","depends_on":["scn_showdown_at_the_span"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Debts Repaid","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_pays","title":"Kael Pays","summary":"Kael stands before the Cartel and the Wardens, accepts the wind-debt for his part in the delayed supplies, and repays it in labour at Emberroost.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Accept responsibility and repair the damage his monopoly push caused.","conflict":"The Cartel factions resent the loss of their leverage and Kael must give up the control he once believed was worth any cost.","outcome":"Kael learns control costs more than it gains and begins repaying his debt, and Veya agrees to share her charts with both factions.","depends_on":["scn_the_bridge_holds"]},{"id":"scn_the_hollow_levy_eased","title":"The Levy Eased","summary":"With the altered ledger as proof, the Cartel withdraws the false grain levy. Maris returns to The Hollow and finally brings the book's truth to her community.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Free The Hollow from the false levy and restore its trade.","conflict":"Some Hollow farmers distrust the Cartel's retreat and want to keep smuggling.","outcome":"Maris realises hiding can be as brave as standing still, chooses to stay and guard the ledger openly, and The Hollow's grain flows again.","depends_on":["scn_the_bridge_holds"]},{"id":"scn_charts_shared","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya publishes her corrected charts and the ledger's findings openly, giving credit to Maris and the clerks who helped, and honours her mentor's theory.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Share the charts so every isle can plan for the drifting bridges.","conflict":"Her fear of becoming like the cartel leaders clashes with her wish for recognition, and the mentor's theory is only partly proven.","outcome":"Veya learns some truths are safer shared than hoarded, and the isles begin charting a safe route together.","depends_on":["scn_kael_pays","scn_the_hollow_levy_eased"]}]}]}
</Output>
