 be used against the Cartel.","conflict":"Open flame is forbidden outside the forge-pits, so Kael's enforcers cannot use fire to intimidate them, and Kael's admiration for Veya makes him hesitate to harm her.","outcome":"Maris leads Veya out through unmapped service corridors, but Kael keeps one torn page, learning that someone inside the Cartel forged the debts.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_forge"]},{"id":"scn_kael_doubts","title":"A Price Too High","summary":"Back at Mistral Docks, Kael confronts the clerk who gave him the levy tip and realises a Cartel rival used his own monopoly push to cover the murder and the forgery.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Identify who forged the debts inside the Cartel.","conflict":"Naming the culprit would break the Cartel's unity, which conflicts with his goal of securing the monopoly.","outcome":"Kael learns the killer plans to cut the Mistral Docks span to destroy the evidence, and he chooses to warn Veya through a rival's channel rather than use the knowledge for himself.","depends_on":["scn_kael_tracks_the_ledger"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_confession","title":"The Wrong Chart","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and finds that her own charts, which she refused to correct earlier, misplaced the failing span. Admitting the error is painful, but it reveals where the killer will strike.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Chart a safe route to protect the spans before they collapse.","conflict":"Veya's flaw delays her acceptance of the error, and Maris, fearing betrayal, threatens to leave with the ledger.","outcome":"Veya admits she was wrong, earns Maris's cautious trust, and they race to Mistral Docks with the corrected chart and the ledger.","depends_on":["scn_kael_doubts","scn_torn_pages"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Span Breaks","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_showdown_at_the_span","title":"Showdown at the Span","summary":"On the Mistral Docks skybridge, Veya, Maris and Kael confront the Cartel factor who forged the debts and killed the toll keeper. The span is rigged to be severed by a single spark.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Expose the killer with the ledger and stop the span from being cut.","conflict":"The killer holds a hidden spark-lamp against the no-open-flame rule, and Kael must choose between protecting Cartel unity and the truth, while Veya fears the ledger will make her as ambitious as the Cartel.","outcome":"Veya reads the corrected wind-sight warning, Maris leads the crowd off the span through the service corridors, and Kael publicly reads the forged entries, which exposes the killer.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_confession","scn_kael_doubts"]},{"id":"scn_the_bridge_holds","title":"The Bridge Holds","summary":"As the killer's spark threatens the cables, Veya's chart guides Kael and Maris to shift the load and shield the lamp, and the span holds.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Save the span and the crowd before the spark severs it.","conflict":"Saving the span requires Kael to give up the monopoly leverage the broken bridge would have handed the Cartel.","outcome":"Kael chooses the bridge over control, the killer is seized by Wardens and clerks, and the ledger is recovered intact.","depends_on":["scn_showdown_at_the_span"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Debts Repaid","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_pays","title":"Kael Pays","summary":"Kael stands before the Cartel and the Wardens, accepts the wind-debt for his part in the delayed supplies, and repays it in labour at Emberroost.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Accept responsibility and repair the damage his monopoly push caused.","conflict":"The Cartel factions resent the loss of their leverage and Kael must give up the control he once believed was worth any cost.","outcome":"Kael learns control costs more than it gains and begins repaying his debt, and Veya agrees to share her charts with both factions.","depends_on":["scn_the_bridge_holds"]},{"id":"scn_the_hollow_levy_eased","title":"The Levy Eased","summary":"With the altered ledger as proof, the Cartel withdraws the false grain levy. Maris returns to The Hollow and finally brings the book's truth to her community.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Free The Hollow from the false levy and restore its trade.","conflict":"Some Hollow farmers distrust the Cartel's retreat and want to keep smuggling.","outcome":"Maris realises hiding can be as brave as standing still, chooses to stay and guard the ledger openly, and The Hollow's grain flows again.","depends_on":["scn_the_bridge_holds"]},{"id":"scn_charts_shared","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya publishes her corrected charts and the ledger's findings openly, giving credit to Maris and the clerks who helped, and honours her mentor's theory.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Share the charts so every isle can plan for the drifting bridges.","conflict":"Her fear of becoming like the cartel leaders clashes with her wish for recognition, and the mentor's theory is only partly proven.","outcome":"Veya learns some truths are safer shared than hoarded, and the isles begin charting a safe route together.","depends_on":["scn_kael_pays","scn_the_hollow_levy_eased"]}]}]}
