control he once believed was worth any cost.","outcome":"Kael learns control costs more than it gains and begins repaying his debt, and Veya agrees to share her charts with both factions.","depends_on":["scn_the_bridge_holds"]},{"id":"scn_the_hollow_levy_eased","title":"The Levy Eased","summary":"With the altered ledger as proof, the Cartel withdraws the false grain levy. Maris returns to The Hollow and finally brings the book's truth to her community.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Free The Hollow from the false levy and restore its trade.","conflict":"Some Hollow farmers distrust the Cartel's retreat and want to keep smuggling.","outcome":"Maris realises hiding can be as brave as standing still, chooses to stay and guard the ledger openly, and The Hollow's grain flows again.","depends_on":["scn_the_bridge_holds"]},{"id":"scn_charts_shared","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya publishes her corrected charts and the ledger's findings openly, giving credit to Maris and the clerks who helped, and honours her mentor's theory.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Share the charts so every isle can plan for the drifting bridges.","conflict":"Her fear of becoming like the cartel leaders clashes with her wish for recognition, and the mentor's theory is only partly proven.","outcome":"Veya learns some truths are safer shared than hoarded, and the isles begin charting a safe route together.","depends_on":["scn_kael_pays","scn_the_hollow_levy_eased"]}]}]}
