{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Emberroost Accord","logline":"As the skybridges begin to fail, a stubborn cartographer, a ruthless Cartel toll-master, and a wary Hollow smuggler must broker a truce between the Bridge Wardens, Drift Cartel, and Hollow Circle at Emberroost before the archipelago is cut apart.","theme":"Shared truths hold the realm together where control tears it apart.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"Fraying Cables","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_charts_of_decline","title":"Charts of Decline","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya uses her wind-sight to confirm that several key skybridges are weakening faster than the Wardens admit, supporting her late mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Chart a safe route through the breaking skybridge network and prove the bridges are failing.","conflict":"Her mentor's theory is dismissed by academy elders, and her stubborn refusal to admit her early charts contain errors undermines her credibility.","outcome":"Veya completes a corrected but alarming chart showing only a few stable routes remain, and she decides to carry it to Mistral Docks to learn who controls those routes."},{"id":"scn_toll_master_at_the_docks","title":"The Toll-Master's Ledger","summary":"Kael tightens Cartel tolls at Mistral Docks and discovers rumours that a cartographer is mapping the last stable bridges. He recognises Veya's name from their shared apprenticeship.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Secure the Cartel's monopoly by seizing the last stable skybridge routes.","conflict":"The Wardens accuse him of sabotaging forge-island supplies, and his admiration for Veya conflicts with his need to suppress her work.","outcome":"Kael resolves to obtain Veya's charts by negotiation or leverage, and dispatches enforcers toward the grain isles to squeeze supplies.","depends_on":[]},{"id":"scn_levy_at_the_hollow","title":"Grain Under Levy","summary":"Cartel enforcers arrive at The Hollow to collect the grain levy. Maris hides the silos' true stock and plans a smuggling run.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"Enforcers close in on her routes, and her slow trust makes her reluctant to seek outside help.","outcome":"Maris escapes with a first hidden shipment but learns the enforcers are closing on her service corridors, so she must find allies."},{"id":"scn_meeting_at_the_docks","title":"Wind for Paths","summary":"Veya reaches Mistral Docks, where Kael confronts her and offers to buy her charts. Maris, passing through with smuggled grain, steps in to get Veya away from the Cartel, and the two strike a bargain of wind knowledge for secret paths.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants safe passage and information; Kael wants her charts; Maris wants a route past the enforcers.","conflict":"Kael presses his claim as an old colleague while Veya refuses to let him control her work, and Maris distrusts both of them.","outcome":"Veya refuses to sell, escapes with Maris, and Kael vows to hunt the charts, which deepens the Toll War.","depends_on":["scn_charts_of_decline","scn_toll_master_at_the_docks","scn_levy_at_the_hollow"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Cables Under Strain","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_corridors","title":"The Service Corridors","summary":"Maris leads Veya through the unmapped corridors between windmills and granaries. Veya reads the wind currents and learns that the bridges around The Hollow are also failing.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to extend her chart with Maris's knowledge, and Maris wants to move grain safely.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust and her loyalty to home clash with her growing friendship with Veya, and Veya's pride makes her dismiss Maris's warnings about the enforcers.","outcome":"The chart shows the stable routes converge on Emberroost, and they decide to take the findings to the Bridge Wardens there.","depends_on":["scn_meeting_at_the_docks"]},{"id":"scn_enforcers_close_in","title":"Closing the Net","summary":"Kael uses his ledger-mastery to find the weak points in The Hollow's grain deals and pressures the Hollow Circle with a tightened levy, while pursuing the charts.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to force the Hollow Circle to reveal where Veya went and to bring them under Cartel terms.","conflict":"Maris refuses to speak and risks her own routes, while Kael's charm and pragmatism hit against her rarely-forgiving loyalty.","outcome":"Maris holds out, but Kael learns Veya is headed for Emberroost and that the Wardens there are short on supplies, so he moves to intercept.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_corridors"]},{"id":"scn_wardens_of_emberroost","title":"The Wardens' Warning","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya presents her charts to the Bridge Wardens. They confirm cloudstone cables are failing and that supplies are short, and they accuse the Cartel of sabotage.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens to act on her charts, and Maris wants the Wardens to oppose the grain levy.","conflict":"The Wardens distrust the Hollow and the Cartel alike, and Veya cannot admit her earlier errors when they point them out.","outcome":"The Wardens agree to hold a parley only if the Cartel and Hollow Circle both attend, and Veya sends word through Maris's contacts.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_corridors"]},{"id":"scn_wind_debt_ambush","title":"Wind-Debt Ambush","summary":"Kael arrives at Emberroost and invokes the wind-debt on Veya's crossings to claim her charts as payment, while Wardens work at the forge-pits.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to claim the charts through wind-debt, and Veya wants to keep them.","conflict":"The wind-debt rule gives Kael a legal claim, and Veya's pride keeps her from admitting she cannot repay it in time.","outcome":"Veya offers to repay in labour at the forge instead, and Kael agrees to attend the parley to watch her.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_close_in","scn_wardens_of_emberroost"]},{"id":"scn_spark_in_the_forge","title":"A Spark in the Forge","summary":"During preparations, a spark escapes a shielded forge-pit and nearly severs a key skybridge cable. Suspicion falls on the Cartel, and Veya's wind-sight lets her spot the real weakness before the cable fails.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Everyone wants to save the cable, and each wants to avoid blame.","conflict":"The Wardens blame Kael while Kael blames the Wardens' neglect, and Maris's old distrust threatens to break the fragile alliance.","outcome":"Veya and Kael cooperate to save the cable, which shows both sides that the bridges will fail without a truce, and the parley goes ahead.","depends_on":["scn_wind_debt_ambush"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Accord","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_parley_opens","title":"Three Banners at the Forge","summary":"The Bridge Wardens, Drift Cartel, and Hollow Circle gather at Emberroost. Veya lays out the charts, Kael defends the tolls and Maris speaks for the Hollow.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Forge a truce that keeps the stable routes open for all three factions.","conflict":"Kael demands exclusive control of the stable routes, Maris demands an end to the grain levy, and Veya must choose between hoarding her charts and sharing them.","outcome":"The talks deadlock when Kael proposes buying the charts outright, which forces Veya to decide.","depends_on":["scn_spark_in_the_forge"]},{"id":"scn_the_choice","title":"Truths Shared","summary":"Veya admits her earlier errors and publicly shares her complete charts. Kael sees that controlling the routes will cost more than shared stewardship would, and he drops his claim.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Break the deadlock and sign a truce.","conflict":"Veya's pride and Kael's belief that price equals worth both resist the change, and Maris must decide whether to trust either of them.","outcome":"Kael waives the wind-debt and levy in exchange for Warden-maintained routes, Maris vouches for the deal for the Hollow, and the Accord is signed.","depends_on":["scn_parley_opens"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"After the Accord","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_cables_rewoven","title":"Cables Rewoven","summary":"Under the Accord, Wardens, Cartel labour and Hollow grain are pooled at Emberroost to braid new cloudstone cables for the failing bridges, with Veya's charts guiding the work.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Begin reinforcing the stable routes under the Accord.","conflict":"Old resentments between Wardens and Cartel crews flare, and Kael struggles to loosen his grip on control.","outcome":"Kael accepts shared oversight, and the first reinforced bridge holds, which proves the Accord can work.","depends_on":["scn_the_choice"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"A Fed Archipelago","summary":"Grain moves openly from The Hollow along the secured routes, and Maris finally stops smuggling and chooses to rely on others.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Deliver grain safely and openly under the Accord.","conflict":"Maris must decide whether to trust the Accord after years of hiding, and Veya must keep the charts updated without claiming sole credit.","outcome":"Maris accepts that hiding was brave but standing openly is stronger, and her friendship with Veya is secured.","depends_on":["scn_cables_rewoven"]},{"id":"scn_new_charts","title":"The Drift Continues","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya publishes her charts openly and honours her mentor, while Kael sends the Cartel's ledgers to be audited alongside them.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants her mentor's theory recognised and the charts made public, and Kael wants to rebuild the Cartel's place in the new order.","conflict":"Academy elders resist the theory, and Kael's pride resists the audit.","outcome":"The theory is accepted and the isles keep drifting but now stay linked through shared upkeep, while Veya and Kael settle into wary respect.","depends_on":["scn_cables_rewoven","scn_hollow_harvest"]}]}]}
