endship with Veya, and Veya's pride makes her dismiss Maris's warnings about the enforcers.","outcome":"The chart shows the stable routes converge on Emberroost, and they decide to take the findings to the Bridge Wardens there.","depends_on":["scn_meeting_at_the_docks"]},{"id":"scn_enforcers_close_in","title":"Closing the Net","summary":"Kael uses his ledger-mastery to find the weak points in The Hollow's grain deals and pressures the Hollow Circle with a tightened levy, while pursuing the charts.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to force the Hollow Circle to reveal where Veya went and to bring them under Cartel terms.","conflict":"Maris refuses to speak and risks her own routes, while Kael's charm and pragmatism hit against her rarely-forgiving loyalty.","outcome":"Maris holds out, but Kael learns Veya is headed for Emberroost and that the Wardens there are short on supplies, so he moves to intercept.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_corridors"]},{"id":"scn_wardens_of_emberroost","title":"The Wardens' Warning","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya presents her charts to the Bridge Wardens. They confirm cloudstone cables are failing and that supplies are short, and they accuse the Cartel of sabotage.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens to act on her charts, and Maris wants the Wardens to oppose the grain levy.","conflict":"The Wardens distrust the Hollow and the Cartel alike, and Veya cannot admit her earlier errors when they point them out.","outcome":"The Wardens agree to hold a parley only if the Cartel and Hollow Circle both attend, and Veya sends word through Maris's contacts.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_corridors"]},{"id":"scn_wind_debt_ambush","title":"Wind-Debt Ambush","summary":"Kael arrives at Emberroost and invokes the wind-debt on Veya's crossings to claim her charts as payment, while Wardens work at the forge-pits.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to claim the charts through wind-debt, and Veya wants to keep them.","conflict":"The wind-debt rule gives Kael a legal claim, and Veya's pride keeps her from admitting she cannot repay it in time.","outcome":"Veya offers to repay in labour at the forge instead, and Kael agrees to attend the parley to watch her.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_close_in","scn_wardens_of_emberroost"]},{"id":"scn_spark_in_the_forge","title":"A Spark in the Forge","summary":"During preparations, a spark escapes a shielded forge-pit and nearly severs a key skybridge cable. Suspicion falls on the Cartel, and Veya's wind-sight lets her spot the real weakness before the cable fails.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Everyone wants to save the cable, and each wants to avoid blame.","conflict":"The Wardens blame Kael while Kael blames the Wardens' neglect, and Maris's old distrust threatens to break the fragile alliance.","outcome":"Veya and Kael cooperate to save the cable, which shows both sides that the bridges will fail without a truce, and the parley goes ahead.","depends_on":["scn_wind_debt_ambush"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Accord","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_parley_opens","title":"Three Banners at the Forge","summary":"The Bridge Wardens, Drift Cartel, and Hollow Circle gather at Emberroost. Veya lays out the charts, Kael defends the tolls and Maris speaks for the Hollow.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Forge a truce that keeps the stable routes open for all three factions.","conflict":"Kael demands exclusive control of the stable routes, Maris demands an end to the grain levy, and Veya must choose between hoarding her charts and sharing them.","outcome":"The talks deadlock when Kael proposes buying the charts outright, which forces Veya to decide.","depends_on":["scn_spark_in_the_forge"]