llow","title":"Grain Under Levy","summary":"Cartel enforcers arrive at The Hollow to collect the grain levy. Maris hides the silos' true stock and plans a smuggling run.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Smuggle enough grain to keep The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"Enforcers close in on her routes, and her slow trust makes her reluctant to seek outside help.","outcome":"Maris escapes with a first hidden shipment but learns the enforcers are closing on her service corridors, so she must find allies."},{"id":"scn_meeting_at_the_docks","title":"Wind for Paths","summary":"Veya reaches Mistral Docks, where Kael confronts her and offers to buy her charts. Maris, passing through with smuggled grain, steps in to get Veya away from the Cartel, and the two strike a bargain of wind knowledge for secret paths.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants safe passage and information; Kael wants her charts; Maris wants a route past the enforcers.","conflict":"Kael presses his claim as an old colleague while Veya refuses to let him control her work, and Maris distrusts both of them.","outcome":"Veya refuses to sell, escapes with Maris, and Kael vows to hunt the charts, which deepens the Toll War.","depends_on":["scn_charts_of_decline","scn_toll_master_at_the_docks","scn_levy_at_the_hollow"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Cables Under Strain","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_corridors","title":"The Service Corridors","summary":"Maris leads Veya through the unmapped corridors between windmills and granaries. Veya reads the wind currents and learns that the bridges around The Hollow are also failing.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to extend her chart with Maris's knowledge, and Maris wants to move grain safely.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust and her loyalty to home clash with her growing friendship with Veya, and Veya's pride makes her dismiss Maris's warnings about the enforcers.","outcome":"The chart shows the stable routes converge on Emberroost, and they decide to take the findings to the Bridge Wardens there.","depends_on":["scn_meeting_at_the_docks"]},{"id":"scn_enforcers_close_in","title":"Closing the Net","summary":"Kael uses his ledger-mastery to find the weak points in The Hollow's grain deals and pressures the Hollow Circle with a tightened levy, while pursuing the charts.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to force the Hollow Circle to reveal where Veya went and to bring them under Cartel terms.","conflict":"Maris refuses to speak and risks her own routes, while Kael's charm and pragmatism hit against her rarely-forgiving loyalty.","outcome":"Maris holds out, but Kael learns Veya is headed for Emberroost and that the Wardens there are short on supplies, so he moves to intercept.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_corridors"]},{"id":"scn_wardens_of_emberroost","title":"The Wardens' Warning","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya presents her charts to the Bridge Wardens. They confirm cloudstone cables are failing and that supplies are short, and they accuse the Cartel of sabotage.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens to act on her charts, and Maris wants the Wardens to oppose the grain levy.","conflict":"The Wardens distrust the Hollow and the Cartel alike, and Veya cannot admit her earlier errors when they point them out.","outcome":"The Wardens agree to hold a parley only if the Cartel and Hollow Circle both attend, and Veya sends word through Maris's contacts.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_corridors"]},{"id":"scn_wind_debt_ambush","title":"Wind-Debt Ambush","summary":"Kael arrives at Emberroost and invokes the wind-debt on Veya's crossings to claim her charts as payment, while Wardens work at the forge-pits.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to claim the charts through wind-debt, and Veya wants to keep them.","conflict":"The wind-debt rule gives Kael a legal claim, and Veya's pride keeps her from admitting she cannot repay it in time.","outcome":"Veya offers to repay in labour at the forge instead, and Kael agrees to attend the parley to watch her.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_close_in","scn_wardens_of_emberroost"]},{"id":"scn_spark_in_the_forge","title":"A Spark in the Forge","summary":"During preparations, a spark escapes a shielded forge-pit and nearly severs a key skybridge cable. Suspicion falls on the Cartel, and Veya's wind-sight lets her spot the real weakness before the cable fails.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Everyone wants to save the cable, and each wants to avoid blame.","conflict":"The Wardens blame Kael while Kael blames the Wardens' neglect, and Maris's old distrust threatens to break the fragile alliance.","outcome":"Veya and Kael cooperate to save the cable, which shows both sides that the bridges will fail without a truce, and the parley goes ahead.","depends_on":["scn_wind_debt_ambush"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Accord","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_parley_opens","title":"Three Banners at the Forge","summary":"The Bridge Wardens, Drift Cartel, and Hollow Circle gather at Emberroost. Veya lays out the charts, Kael defends the tolls and Maris speaks for the Hollow.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Forge a truce that keeps the stable routes open for all three factions.","conflict":"Kael demands exclusive control of the stable routes, Maris demands an end to the grain levy, and Veya must choose between hoarding her charts and sharing them.","outcome":"The talks deadlock when Kael proposes buying the charts outright, which forces Veya to decide.","depends_on":["scn_spark_in_the_forge"]