{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Isle of Lost Wings","logline":"As the skybridges fail, cartographer Veya must chart a safe route before Kael and the Drift Cartel seize the last stable crossings and bury her charts, forcing her to choose between hoarding her truth and sharing it with an archipelago on the brink.","theme":"Truths are safer shared than hoarded.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"Fading Bridges","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_charts","title":"The Fading Charts","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya uses her wind-sight to confirm that several skybridges are failing faster than her late mentor predicted, and that the isles really are drifting apart.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Chart a safe route through the breaking skybridge network and prove her mentor's theory.","conflict":"Her readings contradict the Academy's official charts, and her stubborn refusal to double-check her early calculations leaves a flaw in her first route.","outcome":"Veya completes a draft chart showing one stable route, but it contains an error she will not acknowledge, and she resolves to take it to the Bridge Wardens."},{"id":"scn_docks_offer","title":"Ledgers at Mistral Docks","summary":"Veya travels to Mistral Docks to book passage and is met by Kael, her former fellow apprentice, who offers to buy her charts and sees at once how valuable they are.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants passage to Emberroost; Kael wants to acquire her charts to secure the Cartel's monopoly on the last stable routes.","conflict":"Kael's charm and ledger-mastery press her to sell, while Veya fears becoming like the ambitious cartel leaders and refuses.","outcome":"Veya refuses to sell, and Kael lets her sail while quietly ordering enforcers to watch her and block her route, which sets the Toll War in motion.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_charts"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Tolls and Secret Paths","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_wardens","title":"The Forge-Pits of Emberroost","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya shows her chart to the Bridge Wardens, who accuse Kael of sabotaging forge-island supplies and want to use her route. A warden tests the chart and finds her error; Veya angrily denies it.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Win the Wardens' backing and the cloudstone cable needed to reinforce her route.","conflict":"The Wardens discover the flaw in her chart, and Veya cannot admit she is wrong, so they withhold cable until it is verified.","outcome":"Veya leaves without cable, humiliated and short of time, and learns that Cartel enforcers followed her from the docks.","depends_on":["scn_docks_offer"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_maris","title":"Grain and Maps in The Hollow","summary":"Chased by enforcers, Veya takes refuge in The Hollow, where Maris hides her among the windmills and agrees to trade her secret service corridors for Veya's wind-current knowledge.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya needs a hidden path to evade the Cartel; Maris needs to keep her grain smuggling routes alive against the levy.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya will bring the Cartel down on her isle, while Veya's secrecy about her chart's flaw deepens the mistrust.","outcome":"Maris agrees to an alliance and shares her unmapped corridors, which let Veya correct her route, though Maris warns that she will not forgive betrayal.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_wardens"]},{"id":"scn_docks_ambush","title":"The Levy at Mistral Docks","summary":"Maris and Veya carry grain to Mistral Docks, where Kael has imposed a levy and seized the shipping lanes. He recognises Veya's corrected route in the grain manifest and confronts her.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to get grain and charts through; Kael wants to seize the last stable routes.","conflict":"Kael's ledger-mastery exposes the weakest point in their arrangement, and Veya's pride keeps her from heeding Maris's warning to retreat.","outcome":"Kael impounds the grain and takes a copy of the corrected chart, but he admits privately that he admires Veya's work; Maris loses trust in her.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_maris"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_confession","title":"The Mentor's Archive","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya studies her mentor's papers by wind-sight and finds that the stolen chart will lead Cartel ships onto a failing bridge. She finally admits her original error.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to repair her chart and warn the isles; Maris wants to recover the impounded grain.","conflict":"Admitting her mistake threatens Veya's pride and recognition, and Maris must decide whether to forgive her.","outcome":"Veya accepts that the truth must be shared rather than hoarded, and she and Maris resolve to publish the corrected charts and race Kael to the bridge.","depends_on":["scn_docks_ambush"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Breaking Span","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_climax","title":"The Last Stable Bridge","summary":"Kael leads Cartel ships onto the stolen route as the bridge begins to fail. Veya, using wind-sight and Maris's corridors, reaches Emberroost and warns the Wardens and Kael alike, sharing her full corrected chart.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to guide everyone across safely; Kael wants to seize the route before it collapses.","conflict":"Kael's belief that price equals worth makes him refuse to give up control, and Veya must give away the chart she once guarded.","outcome":"Veya shares the chart openly, the Wardens reinforce the span, and Kael sees that control costs more than it gains and stands down.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_confession"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Shared Charts","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_docks_resolution","title":"A New Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael releases the impounded grain and opens the routes under shared terms, repaying part of the wind-debt in goods to the Wardens.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to repair the damage his monopoly caused; Maris wants her isle fed.","conflict":"Cartel merchants resent Kael's concession, and Maris struggles to forgive him.","outcome":"The grain levy is eased and the Cartel accepts shared routes, though tension between Kael and the Wardens remains.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_climax"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_resolution","title":"Charts for All","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and publishes her charts for every isle, crediting her mentor and Maris, while mourning that the isles will keep drifting.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to honour her mentor and make the charts public.","conflict":"Giving up sole credit tests her need for recognition, and the drifting of the isles cannot be undone.","outcome":"Veya accepts shared recognition and her friendship with Maris is restored, and she begins charting the next drift with the whole archipelago's help.","depends_on":["scn_docks_resolution"]}]}]}
